// DIAGNOSIS: The problem is that the SMILES parser accepts single atoms like "C" as complete
// valid SMILES strings. So the model generates "C" and the strategy immediately closes the span.
// The output <<C>> is a valid single-atom SMILES but not an acrylate molecule.
//
// ROOT CAUSE: The constrained span opens immediately (before any free generation),
// and after generating just 1 token the parser considers it complete (single atom = valid SMILES).
// We need to force generation of a sufficiently long acrylate SMILES.
//
// FIX: Use a minimum token count threshold before allowing span closure.
// Specifically, only close the span when |currentConstrainedOut| >= 12 tokens
// (acrylate like "C=CC(=O)OCC" has ~12 tokens). Before that threshold, keep generating.
//
// We can enforce this by checking: only call CloseConstrainedSpan or CloseSpanIfComplete
// when |currentConstrainedOut| >= minLength. Before reaching minLength, always call
// AdaptiveConstrainedStep to continue generating.
//
// BUT: the parser may report IsCompletePrefix = true after 1 token. If we force more tokens,
// we might exit the valid-prefix state. We need to keep generating tokens that maintain
// IsValidPrefix but NOT call Close until we have enough tokens.
//
// Actually the correct approach: use AdaptiveConstrainedStep which hard-masks to parser-valid
// next tokens. After "C", the next valid tokens might include "=" (leading to C=C...).
// So we need to PREVENT early closure, not prevent parser progression.
//
// KEY INSIGHT: The task guidance should prime the LM to generate a long SMILES.
// The minLength guard prevents the span from being closed too early.
// We still need the parser to be able to accept the SMILES once we have enough tokens.
//
// Strategy:
// 1. AppendTaskGuidance with strong acrylate scaffold priming (include the prefix "C=CC(=O)O").
// 2. Open constrained span.
// 3. Generate tokens with AdaptiveConstrainedStep.
// 4. Only allow CloseSpanIfComplete when |currentConstrainedOut| >= 10 tokens.
// 5. At the very end of budget, force closure if complete or rollback to complete prefix.
//
// This should produce full acrylate SMILES strings like "C=CC(=O)OCC" instead of just "C".
// CSD_RATIONALE_END

// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
