// and use IsTokenValidNext to steer toward acrylate structure.
// Also: provide much more specific guidance about the EXACT SMILES to generate.
//
// The "entered_constrained_mode_too_early" failure mode means the evaluator sees
// the constrained span opens too soon. But if we delay opening it, we need some
// preamble text. However, the output contract says "a single SMILES string and nothing else."
// This means NO preamble - just the SMILES.
//
// So the visible << >> span IS the output. We need it to contain a real acrylate SMILES.
// The problem is "C" is valid SMILES but not an acrylate.
//
// THE REAL FIX: We must prevent closure of tiny spans. The minLength approach failed
// because the check !parser.IsCompletePrefix was bypassed. 
// Let's use RollbackAndContinue after detecting a dead-end/tiny generation,
// or simply never call CloseConstrainedSpan until |currentConstrainedOut| >= minLength.
//
