Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The core problem is "entered_constrained_mode_too_early": the strategy opens
// a constrained span immediately, so the LM generates only a 1-token SMILES
// like "O" which is syntactically valid SMILES but not a real isocyanate.
//
// The fix: use ConstrainedGeneration which runs a full parser-guided loop from
// an empty prefix until parser completeness or budget exhaustion, then close the
// span. We use AppendTaskGuidance to steer the LM toward isocyanate structures.
//
// Key insight: ConstrainedGeneration starts from an empty constrained prefix and
// loops until the parser says IsCompletePrefix or EOS or budget. This produces
// a full molecule SMILES rather than a single atom.
//
// After ConstrainedGeneration completes, we reconstruct generated/inside/current
// state by treating the returned sequence as the constrained chunk, then close.
//
// However, ConstrainedGeneration's API: it returns (constrainedGenerated, terminatedByEos)
// where constrainedGenerated is the full sequence of tokens generated inside the
// constrained span. It takes its own internal prompt. We need to open the span
// first, then call ConstrainedGeneration.
//
// Actually re-reading the API: ConstrainedGeneration(lm, parser, prompt, maxSteps, eosToken)
// returns (constrainedGenerated, terminatedByEos). It uses its own internal loop.
// The cost is +|constrainedGenerated| (plus 1 if terminated by EOS).
//
// Problem: we need to track steps for budget. ConstrainedGeneration consumes up
// to maxSteps - steps (remaining budget minus reserve for open/close).
//
// Plan:
// 1. AppendTaskGuidance with strong isocyanate instructions
// 2. OpenConstrainedSpan (costs 1 step)
// 3. Call ConstrainedGeneration with remaining budget - 1 (reserve for CloseConstrainedSpan)
//    BUT ConstrainedGeneration doesn't update our generated/inside/current tracking
//    and we can't directly integrate it with our loop.
//
// Simpler alternative: use a manual loop with AdaptiveConstrainedStep but
// set minTokensBeforeClose high (e.g., 6) and use a larger step budget per
// constrained token. The tiny-span issue is that CloseSpanIfComplete fires
// after 1 token because "O" is a complete SMILES.
//
// The real fix: DO NOT call CloseSpanIfComplete until we have generated at
// least a minimum number of tokens. For isocyanates, O=C=N followed by
// something is at minimum ~4-6 tokens. We need minTokensBeforeClose.
//
// But the previous attempt with minTokensBeforeClose=5 also got 0% accuracy.
// The diagnostic says "tiny_span_rate: 100%" and "visible span token length avg: 1.00"
// This means AppendConstrainedToken is only called ONCE and then something breaks.
//
// Looking at the code flow: CloseSpanIfComplete fires BEFORE the generation step.
// After OpenConstrainedSpan, currentConstrainedOut = []. Parser.IsCompletePrefix([])
// might be true! So CloseSpanIfComplete immediately closes with empty span.
// Then generated = ["<<", ">>"] and the extracted answer is empty → "O" from text fallback?
//
// Actually the diagnostic says "Visible span token length avg: 1.00" so spans have
// 1 token. Something produces 1 token. Let me re-examine.
//
// Looking at prior failing output: "<<O>>" - so the span contains exactly "O".
// This means: OpenConstrainedSpan → "<<", then one ConstrainedStep returns "O",
// AppendConstrainedToken appends "O", then CloseSpanIfComplete fires and "O" is
// a complete SMILES so it closes immediately with ">>".
//
// Fix: We must prevent premature close when the constrained sequence is too short.
// Use a minTokensBeforeClose counter and skip CloseSpanIfComplete until enough tokens.
// But also ensure we don't call it at ALL until minTokensBeforeClose reached.
//
// Additionally: the SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep is first in alternation when
// |currentConstrainedOut| is empty, which calls it with 0-length current. That
// should be fine. But "O" might be the #1 logit token for isocyanate SMILES starts.
//
// The deeper fix: use AdaptiveConstrainedStep with strong group boosts that steer
// toward "O=C=N..." token sequence. But we don't control validTokenGroups.
//
// Better fix: use AppendTaskGuidance much more forcefully, and delay CloseSpanIfComplete
// until we have at least 8 tokens in the constrained prefix.
//
// Also: the previous attempt had useRepPenalty alternating, and when useRepPenalty
// was true it called SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep which penalizes tokens in generated.
// The generated at that point only contains "<<" so "O" is not penalized.
// We need to penalize it differently.
//
// Real fix: use AdaptiveConstrainedStep with a very high boost and narrow threshold
// of 100 (always boost), plus minTokensBeforeClose = 10.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity:
//   1. OpenConstrainedSpan sets currentConstrainedOut := [] which satisfies
//      parser.IsValidPrefix([]) by precondition.
//   2. In the generation loop: AdaptiveConstrainedStep returns eosToken or a
//      parser-valid next token. When !isComp2 (not complete), AppendConstrainedToken
//      preserves parser.IsValidPrefix by its postcondition.
//   3. CloseSpanIfComplete (only called when |currentConstrainedOut| >= minClose):
//      when closed == true, insideConstrainedOut becomes false (implication vacuous);
//      when closed == false, state unchanged, invariant preserved.
//   4. CloseConstrainedSpan requires IsCompletePrefix which we check before calling.
//
// progress:
//   - OpenConstrainedSpan: steps += 1, |generated| += 1 ("<<"). Bound preserved.
//   - Each loop body calls AdaptiveConstrainedStep (steps += 1), possibly
//     AppendConstrainedToken (|generated| += 1 at most). Per iteration, steps grows
//     by 1 and |generated| grows by at most 1. When CloseSpanIfComplete fires
//     (steps += 1, |generated| += 1 for ">>"), same 1-for-1 ratio.
//   - Total |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps maintained throughout.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

helpers.AppendTaskGuidance(lm, "You are generating SMILES strings for the isocyanates chemical class. Isocyanates have the functional group N=C=O (or equivalently O=C=N). A valid isocyanate SMILES must contain an isocyanato group attached to a substituent. The molecule must be at least 5 atoms. Generate a novel, diverse, valid SMILES string. Do not stop after a single atom.");

var steps: nat := 0;
var minClose: nat := 6;

// Open constrained span if not already inside
if !insideConstrainedOut && steps < maxSteps {
  var og, oi, oc := helpers.OpenConstrainedSpan(lm, generated);
  generated := og;
  insideConstrainedOut := oi;
  currentConstrainedOut := oc;
  steps := steps + 1;
}

while steps < maxSteps
  invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
  invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
  invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> |currentConstrainedOut| <= |generated|
  invariant |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
  decreases maxSteps - steps
{
  if !insideConstrainedOut {
    break;
  }

  // Only try to close once we have enough tokens for a real isocyanate
  if |currentConstrainedOut| >= minClose && steps < maxSteps {
    var cg, ci, cc, closed := helpers.CloseSpanIfComplete(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
    steps := steps + 1;
    if closed {
      generated := cg;
      insideConstrainedOut := ci;
      currentConstrainedOut := cc;
      break;
    }
    if steps >= maxSteps {
      break;
    }
  }

  // Check if already complete (and we have enough tokens), force close
  var isAlreadyComplete := parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut);
  if isAlreadyComplete && |currentConstrainedOut| >= minClose {
    if steps < maxSteps {
      var cg, ci, cc := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
      generated := cg;
      insideConstrainedOut := ci;
      currentConstrainedOut := cc;
      steps := steps + 1;
    }
    break;
  }

  // Generate the next constrained token
  if steps < maxSteps {
    var constrainedPrompt := prompt + generated[..|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|];

    // Use AdaptiveConstrainedStep with aggressive boosting (narrowThreshold=200 means always boost)
    var next := helpers.AdaptiveConstrainedStep(
      lm, parser, constrainedPrompt, currentConstrainedOut, validTokenGroups, 5.0, 200, eosToken
    );
    steps := steps + 1;

    if next == eosToken {
      // On EOS: if we have enough tokens and parse is complete, close
      if |currentConstrainedOut| >= minClose {
        var isComp := parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut);
        if isComp && steps < maxSteps {
          var cg, ci, cc := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
          generated := cg;
          insideConstrainedOut := ci;
          currentConstrainedOut := cc;
          steps := steps + 1;
        }
      }
      break;
    } else {
      // Only append if not already at a complete prefix (to avoid precondition violation)
      var isComp2 := parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut);
      if isComp2 {
        // We're complete but got a non-EOS; close if enough tokens
        if |currentConstrainedOut| >= minClose && steps < maxSteps {
          var cg, ci, cc := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
          generated := cg;
          insideConstrainedOut := ci;
          currentConstrainedOut := cc;
          steps := steps + 1;
        }
        break;
      } else {
        var ag, ai, ac := helpers.AppendConstrainedToken(
          lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut, next
        );
        generated := ag;
        insideConstrainedOut := ai;
        currentConstrainedOut := ac;
      }
    }
  }
}

// Final cleanup: if still inside and complete, close
if insideConstrainedOut && steps < maxSteps {
  var isComp := parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut);
  if isComp {
    var cg, ci, cc := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
    generated := cg;
    insideConstrainedOut := ci;
    currentConstrainedOut := cc;
    steps := steps + 1;
  }
}

cost := steps;

